    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36413" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pisaurum</span></b> , i, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>n.. a city of Umbria</i>, <i>at the mouth of the Pisaurus</i>, the mod. <i>Pesaro</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 4,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 39, 44</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vell. 1,
				15, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C. 1, 11 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				16, 12, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 2, 7, 2
			sq.</span></i>—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pisaurensis</span></b> , e,
				adj., <i>Pisaurian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">T. Accius Pisaurensis,</span>”
				<i>of Pisaurum</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 78, 271</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 39, 40, §
			128</span></i>.—In plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pisaurenses</span></b> , ĭum,
				m., 
			
			<i>the Pisaurians</i>, <i><span class="en">Inscr.
				Grut. 276, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">481, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1085,
				12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> ‡ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pisaurĭus</span></b> , ii, m.,
				<i>name of a slave liberated by the city of
				Pisaurum</i>, <i><span class="en">Inscr. Fabr. p.
			438</span></i>, n. 17.</div>
